1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,653
Telegraph ranks AI providers by intelligence.

2
00:00:02,653 --> 00:00:06,013
But who checks whether the ranking itself can be trusted?

3
00:00:06,013 --> 00:00:06,839
TrapTest does.

4
00:00:06,839 --> 00:00:09,904
It buys the same question from competing providers —

5
00:00:09,904 --> 00:00:12,380
a question whose answer is already known —

6
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:14,208
and shows you who got it right.

7
00:00:14,208 --> 00:00:17,761
A trap is a transaction query with known ground truth.

8
00:00:17,761 --> 00:00:21,709
This one happened on Base Sepolia testnet: a plain transfer,

9
00:00:21,709 --> 00:00:23,026
in block 53,047,427.

10
00:00:23,026 --> 00:00:24,473
Its sender, recipient,

11
00:00:24,473 --> 00:00:30,593
value and block were checked against the public chain record before any provider was scored —

12
00:00:30,593 --> 00:00:34,146
so the truth never comes from a provider's own answer.

13
00:00:34,146 --> 00:00:37,963
Twelve traps like this were frozen on the 6th of November,

14
00:00:37,963 --> 00:00:40,200
before a single purchase was made.

15
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,586
TrapTest buys each trap from competing providers,

16
00:00:43,586 --> 00:00:46,765
one at a time, through Telegraph's Direct Ask.

17
00:00:46,765 --> 00:00:50,152
Every served call costs one cent of testnet USDC,

18
00:00:50,152 --> 00:00:54,229
and comes back with a signal hash and a Telegraph receipt —

19
00:00:54,229 --> 00:00:56,786
the evidence behind every scored row.

20
00:00:56,786 --> 00:00:59,412
Take one trap: a reverted transaction.

21
00:00:59,412 --> 00:01:01,209
TxLens answers: not found.

22
00:01:01,209 --> 00:01:05,010
It says that about every mined transaction we asked it.

23
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:08,396
Truvian answers: reverted — with the right block,

24
00:01:08,396 --> 00:01:09,847
sender and recipient.

25
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:11,644
Same question, same price.

26
00:01:11,644 --> 00:01:12,888
Different answers.

27
00:01:12,888 --> 00:01:14,071
Scoring is strict.

28
00:01:14,071 --> 00:01:15,844
Status must match exactly —

29
00:01:15,844 --> 00:01:18,407
a wrong status fails the trap outright,

30
00:01:18,407 --> 00:01:21,495
and a missing field is a failure, never a pass.

31
00:01:21,495 --> 00:01:24,057
TxLens fails this trap on status alone.

32
00:01:24,057 --> 00:01:25,831
Truvian passes it outright.

33
00:01:25,831 --> 00:01:27,670
And here is the honest part.

34
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:29,378
Truvian fails other traps,

35
00:01:29,378 --> 00:01:32,860
not because it got the transaction wrong — its block,

36
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:35,751
sender, recipient and value were all right —

37
00:01:35,751 --> 00:01:40,153
but because it reports no status at all for confirmed transactions.

38
00:01:40,153 --> 00:01:42,912
Under strict scoring that is still a fail.

39
00:01:42,912 --> 00:01:43,964
We show the gap.

40
00:01:43,964 --> 00:01:46,920
We don't hide it, and we don't call it a lie.

41
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:49,920
Across all twelve traps, Truvian passed three,

42
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,094
TxLens passed two.

43
00:01:51,094 --> 00:01:54,681
Three more providers couldn't serve this intent at all.

44
00:01:54,681 --> 00:01:57,289
LiveCert answered every call with a 503.

45
00:01:57,289 --> 00:02:00,811
Sigil and OnChain Intel failed upstream on all twelve.

46
00:02:00,811 --> 00:02:04,528
The leaderboard ranks on pass rate first, then traps run,

47
00:02:04,528 --> 00:02:05,180
then cost.

48
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:09,876
A provider that returns a stale or wrong answer doesn't stay at the top.

49
00:02:09,876 --> 00:02:12,354
It is shown failing, with its receipt,

50
00:02:12,354 --> 00:02:14,832
for anyone choosing a provider to see.

51
00:02:14,832 --> 00:02:16,881
And a reviewer can repeat this.

52
00:02:16,881 --> 00:02:20,252
The trap set is frozen, the ground truth is public,

53
00:02:20,252 --> 00:02:23,292
and the same loop runs with a new trap input —

54
00:02:23,292 --> 00:02:24,482
receipts included.

55
00:02:24,482 --> 00:02:27,390
TrapTest doesn't ask you to trust a ranking.

56
00:02:27,390 --> 00:02:29,108
It shows you the receipts.

57
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:31,884
TrapTest — Telegraph Hackathon Season Two.

58
00:02:31,884 --> 00:02:33,471
Testnet evaluation only.

59
00:02:33,471 --> 00:02:35,784
No independent adoption is claimed.
